# Line-ending policy
#
# Compute gold fixtures embed an `input_digest` = sha256 of the *input file's raw
# bytes*. If git rewrites line endings on checkout (core.autocrlf=true), that
# digest no longer matches what the engine computes, and the gold reproduction
# test fails for reasons unrelated to the code. Pinning fixtures to LF keeps the
# digest stable across machines and checkouts.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: only the compute fixtures, which are the files
# whose bytes feed a hash. Wider rules would rewrite unrelated files.

domains/lubricant/fixtures/** text eol=lf
